# ShaderCandy Linux Package

This directory contains the Debian packaging configuration for ShaderCandy.

## Building the Package

### Prerequisites

```bash
sudo apt-get install build-essential debhelper cmake libx11-dev \
                     libgl1-mesa-dev libglu1-mesa-dev libxss-dev
```

### Quick Build

```bash
cd linux
./build-deb.sh
```

### Manual Build

```bash
# From project root
cd ..
dpkg-buildpackage -us -uc -b

# Or using debuild
debuild -us -uc -b
```

## Installing

```bash
sudo dpkg -i ../shadercandy_1.0.0-1_amd64.deb

# If dependencies are missing:
sudo apt-get install -f
```

## Files

- `debian/control` - Package metadata and dependencies
- `debian/rules` - Build rules
- `debian/changelog` - Version history
- `debian/copyright` - License information
- `debian/install` - Installation manifest
- `debian/postinst` - Post-installation script
- `debian/postrm` - Post-removal script
- `shadercandy.desktop` - Desktop entry
- `shadercandy.1` - Man page

## XScreenSaver Integration

The package automatically registers with xscreensaver if installed.
To manually add ShaderCandy to xscreensaver:

1. Edit `~/.xscreensaver`
2. Add to the `programs:` section:
   ```
   glsl: "ShaderCandy" shadercandy-screensaver -root\n\
   ```

## Custom Shaders

Place custom `.frag` files in:
- `~/.local/share/shadercandy/shaders/`
- `/usr/local/share/shadercandy/shaders/`

## Troubleshooting

### Black Screen
- Ensure OpenGL 3.3+ is supported by your GPU
- Check `glxinfo | grep "OpenGL version"`

### Missing Shaders
- Verify shaders are in `/usr/share/shadercandy/shaders/`
- Use `-shader-dir` option to specify custom path

### Build Errors
- Ensure all build dependencies are installed
- Check CMake version is >= 3.20

